WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.617
The NumPy where function applies conditional logic across an array.

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:11.998
Think of it as saying: if this condition is true, use one value; otherwise, use another value.

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:19.634
For example, we might label sales as high or low depending on whether they exceed a threshold.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:27.374
Instead of looping through every value, the NumPy where function performs the decision across the entire array.

00:00:27.374 --> 00:00:33.779
This pattern is useful for creating categories, flags, and transformed values.

00:00:33.779 --> 00:00:41.174
When reading the code, focus first on the condition, then identify the value used for true cases and the value used for

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.666
false cases.
